  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="main-content">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cat care FAQ</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Answers to common questions about cats</h1>
        <p>
          Learn the basics of cat behavior, diet, sleep, and play with a quick FAQ
          designed like a polished product help page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="faq-panel" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
        <div class="faq-list">
          <div class="example">
            <h2 class="question">
              <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1">
                Why do cats purr?
                <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div class="details" id="faq-1" hidden>
              <p>
                Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and content, but they can also
                purr to self-soothe when stressed, recovering, or seeking comfort from
                a person they trust.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <h2 class="question">
              <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
                How much do cats sleep?
                <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div class="details" id="faq-2" hidden>
              <p>
                Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and
                senior cats may sleep even more because their bodies need extra rest.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <h2 class="question">
              <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
                Why do cats knead with their paws?
                <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div class="details" id="faq-3" hidden>
              <p>
                Kneading starts in kittenhood while nursing, and many cats keep the
                habit into adulthood. It usually signals comfort, security, or a way to
                mark a favorite spot with scent glands in their paws.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <h2 class="question">
              <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
                What should cats eat every day?
                <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div class="details" id="faq-4" hidden>
              <p>
                Cats are obligate carnivores, so they need a balanced cat food with
                high-quality animal protein, essential fats, and nutrients such as
                taurine. Fresh water should always be available too.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <h2 class="question">
              <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
                How can I keep an indoor cat entertained?
                <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div class="details" id="faq-5" hidden>
              <p>
                Rotate toys, add scratching posts, provide climbing spots, and schedule
                short interactive play sessions. Window perches and puzzle feeders also
                help keep indoor cats mentally engaged.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
